{"generatedAt":"2026-10-14T14:57:43.839Z","answers":[{"id":"5FQA9pvM8YQpNHa0blLM","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Lily htike","userId":"05247060869811950575","questionIndex":8,"answerContent":"The Buddha did his missionary work out of deep compassion to help people end their suffering, understand the truth, and find true peace","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-08-28T00:49:10.905Z"},{"id":"93aLidVpDaxamH0D2WfC","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Lily htike","userId":"05247060869811950575","questionIndex":5,"answerContent":"The Buddha preached to the 30 Bhaddavaggiya princes. When they came looking for a woman who stole their gold, the Buddha asked them, \"Is it better to look for a lost woman or to look for yourselves?\" The princes replied that it was better to look for themselves. The Buddha then taught them the Dhamma, and they all became monks.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-08-28T00:45:36.702Z"},{"id":"9xdKxy0uqLsJKvwoHNQZ","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Lily htike","userId":"05247060869811950575","questionIndex":12,"answerContent":"showing kindness, speaking politely, and respecting elders. By learning the Buddha's teachings, meditating to keep a peaceful mind, and setting a positive example for others, they naturally help keep the Dhamma alive and strong in their daily lives.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-08-28T00:56:08.777Z"},{"id":"A2mQuU7l3iN2sUZ0uXkA","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Mabel Naing","userId":"16685285020362320583","questionIndex":8,"answerContent":"To spread the word of the Dhamma.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-07-17T20:27:07.098Z"},{"id":"A9p4T83flIZCE8hyS9D1","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Lily htike","userId":"05247060869811950575","questionIndex":3,"answerContent":"He taught the five former companions and he taught it at the deer park in Isipatana","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-08-28T00:42:08.887Z"},{"id":"AmU0x9vgBdWr823rDpSt","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Mabel Naing","userId":"16685285020362320583","questionIndex":2,"answerContent":"He taught others about how to reach enlightenment.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-07-17T20:14:09.567Z"},{"id":"B0iS4sbfZgxJoSmw41mi","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Mabel Naing","userId":"16685285020362320583","questionIndex":3,"answerContent":"In the Migadawa Forest, to 5 monks.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-07-17T20:18:13.445Z"},{"id":"DJaSiIG7GbLWzr3A8aVi","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Mabel Naing","userId":"16685285020362320583","questionIndex":10,"answerContent":"To spread the word for a cause.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-07-17T20:28:56.136Z"},{"id":"FOFzXHndhBBucWA0nYsJ","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Lily htike","userId":"05247060869811950575","questionIndex":7,"answerContent":"the five former companions Yasa and his fifty-four friends, and the thirty princes.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-08-28T00:47:35.095Z"},{"id":"FfAZIESYXrkTilEGdREm","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Mabel Naing","userId":"16685285020362320583","questionIndex":1,"answerContent":"To reach enlightenment, and help all living creatures reach it too.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-07-17T20:12:49.827Z"},{"id":"Fl027207GdaJivvsuwT0","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Lily htike","userId":"05247060869811950575","questionIndex":2,"answerContent":"He stayed near the Bodhi Tree and spended 49 days to reflect on his new wisdom and enjoy the peace of Enlightenment","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-08-28T00:38:39.063Z"},{"id":"HBdc2zGiajI3NYu7tG3E","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Lily htike","userId":"05247060869811950575","questionIndex":11,"answerContent":"by walking from village to village to teach the Dhamma to anyone willing to listen","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-08-28T00:54:18.993Z"},{"id":"HchQjyu90zwBKe6GJLL3","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Lily htike","userId":"05247060869811950575","questionIndex":9,"answerContent":"spreading the Buddha’s teachings","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-08-28T00:50:42.048Z"},{"id":"KNo6Lqnaohk7EBQ9X7O6","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Lily htike","userId":"05247060869811950575","questionIndex":6,"answerContent":"all thirty princes attained noble stages of Enlightenment","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-08-28T00:46:42.059Z"},{"id":"M9oZOXc0Rlp2pKIkpCKS","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Mabel Naing","userId":"16685285020362320583","questionIndex":7,"answerContent":"The 5 monks, the rich man and his 54 friends, and the 30 princes.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-07-17T20:24:44.399Z"},{"id":"VFtzXUYBZOaiyvCi5dRH","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Lily htike","userId":"05247060869811950575","questionIndex":4,"answerContent":"60 Arahants","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-08-28T00:43:07.421Z"},{"id":"VpxOrq3lmHcJrLolAT6R","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Mabel Naing","userId":"16685285020362320583","questionIndex":11,"answerContent":"They preach the Dhamma and hold sermons.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-07-17T20:29:55.279Z"},{"id":"g4aiQ4EQcNPQpvzTouMp","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Mabel Naing","userId":"16685285020362320583","questionIndex":5,"answerContent":"The Buddha preached to the 30 princes the importance of finding oneself, and they became monks after.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-07-17T20:22:28.238Z"},{"id":"gnEnBNIrChs4iMkRrBZb","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Lily htike","userId":"05247060869811950575","questionIndex":10,"answerContent":"so that the teachings of the Dhamma could reach people in different regions.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-08-28T00:51:25.959Z"},{"id":"gyBHTnRUgG5aOq7WJFgQ","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Mabel Naing","userId":"16685285020362320583","questionIndex":12,"answerContent":"We can tell others about Buddhism and the values they should follow.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-07-17T20:30:36.787Z"},{"id":"kra4KS1sAxKxvwfAyo1E","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Lily htike","userId":"05247060869811950575","questionIndex":1,"answerContent":"He did it out of love and compassion to save all living beings from suffering and lead them to peace.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-08-28T00:37:30.306Z"},{"id":"qfEaC8DPunG4bBsT54zS","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Mabel Naing","userId":"16685285020362320583","questionIndex":6,"answerContent":"They became monks.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-07-17T20:23:01.206Z"},{"id":"qtZ4po1f36v7IFH5K7fH","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Mabel Naing","userId":"16685285020362320583","questionIndex":4,"answerContent":"60 monks.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-07-17T20:19:30.667Z"},{"id":"wGA1MRlhJDzaBrH44Z3v","lessonId":"z0dqm3K43xTDI2NJLD8I","studentName":"Mabel Naing","userId":"16685285020362320583","questionIndex":9,"answerContent":"It means spreading the word for a cause.","likes":[],"timestamp":"2026-07-17T20:27:55.688Z"}]}